{"name":"Dubarry","hex":"#f25f66","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Madame du Barry","blocks":[{"text":"Jeanne Bécu, Comtesse du Barry was the last maîtresse-en-titre of King Louis XV of France. She was executed by guillotine during the French Revolution on accusations of treason—particularly being suspected of assisting émigrés to flee from the Revolution. She is also known as \"Mademoiselle Vaubernier\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/%C3%89lisabeth_Vig%C3%A9e-Lebrun_-_Madame_du_Barry.jpg/330px-%C3%89lisabeth_Vig%C3%A9e-Lebrun_-_Madame_du_Barry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madame_du_Barry"},{"title":"DuBarry (film)","blocks":[{"text":"DuBarry is a lost 1915 silent film historical drama based on David Belasco's 1901 play Du Barry. The play itself is adapted from the novel Memoirs d'un médicin by Alexandre Dumas. Mrs. Leslie Carter reprises her role from the Broadway play."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/The_theatre_through_its_stage_door_%281919%29_%2814578398407%29.jpg/330px-The_theatre_through_its_stage_door_%281919%29_%2814578398407%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DuBarry_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/%C3%89lisabeth_Vig%C3%A9e-Lebrun_-_Madame_du_Barry.jpg/500px-%C3%89lisabeth_Vig%C3%A9e-Lebrun_-_Madame_du_Barry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/%C3%89lisabeth_Vig%C3%A9e-Lebrun_-_Madame_du_Barry.jpg/1280px-%C3%89lisabeth_Vig%C3%A9e-Lebrun_-_Madame_du_Barry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/%C3%89lisabeth_Vig%C3%A9e-Lebrun_-_Madame_d